# The Apple SDK the macOS application is linked against. It is not free
# software: it is in no repository and in no image, and the build never
# downloads it. Whoever builds makes it from Xcode, with the scripts
# below, and the build refuses a file whose hash is not the one here.
# See docs/REPRODUCIBLE-BUILDS.md.
#
# Xcode 26.1.1 (build 17B100), from Apple, with an Apple ID:
#   https://developer.apple.com/download/all/?q=Xcode%2026.1.1
f4c65b01e2807372b61553c71036dbfef492d7c79d4c380a5afb61aa1018e555  Xcode_26.1.1_Apple_silicon.xip
# What gen-sdk.py makes of it: the macOS 26.1 SDK and the libc++ headers,
# every date zeroed, every owner root. The same file Bitcoin Core builds
# its releases with.
9600fa93644df674ee916b5e2c8a6ba8dacf631996a65dc922d003b98b5ea3b1  Xcode-26.1.1-17B100-extracted-SDK-with-libcxx-headers.tar
# What gen-sdk-cryptexes.py makes of it: WebKit, JavaScriptCore and the
# other frameworks the SDK keeps under System/Cryptexes, which the file
# above only links to. Written the same way, into the same tree.
fb8a938117fc12e5982d77c241f3168bdab9441cecacff51d5de277e66f337f3  Xcode-26.1.1-17B100-extracted-SDK-cryptexes.tar
#
# The two scripts, copied byte for byte from the Bitcoin Core project
# (MIT licence, see COPYING in this directory):
#   https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/blob/3e01b5d0e7be3dabe7f52d70e577f03f31505ad9/contrib/macdeploy/gen-sdk.py
#   https://github.com/bitcoin-core/apple-sdk-tools/blob/7c5444ceb541c4b75f90ad22dcc5ff4d3cf4bb2d/extract_xcode.py
454c3230f56fccce059d8d4b1cda3dbcdefdd838f20954b86720e9d136e7dcd0  gen-sdk.py
d4053b8fa2c8d789f8f7031a4e34c37e47522e282da4dd03b73589027d5d6c21  extract_xcode.py
